# BuildKit reads <dockerfile-path>.dockerignore in preference to the context
# root's .dockerignore, which is what lets this file live beside the Dockerfile
# it belongs to while the build context stays the repository root.
#
# Requires DOCKER_BUILDKIT=1 (or docker buildx). build.sh sets it.

# Version control and CI metadata: never needed to compile a Go binary, and
# .git in particular is the single largest thing in a normal checkout.
.git
.github
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# The deployment layer builds the images; it is never inside one.
deploy

# Documentation.
docs
**/*.md
LICENSE

# Local build output and state. data/ is where every service's kvstore and
# event log land when run outside a container; shipping a developer's event log
# into an image would be both large and a data leak.
bin
dist
data
**/data
*.out
*.test
coverage*

# Editor and OS noise.
.idea
.vscode
.DS_Store
*.swp

# Anything that could carry a credential. The build never needs one, and an
# accidental commit of a key must not become an accidental push of an image
# containing it.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
.env
.env.*
!deploy/compose/.env.example
